            ]
          },
          "text": "In addition, I would like to also inquire that, what’s the standard of “users who choose GPT-4o each day?”\n\nUsers who are on a streak with sending requests to GPT-4o?\nThen what is the minimum streak to fulfill your standard? 10 days? 30 days? What about those who don’t send requests everyday but still use 4o mostly? How about those who need GPT-4o for certain academic tasks, but are not working during holidays?\n\nAnd what’s the minimum requests that users need to send to fulfill your standard, 1 request is good enough, or 10 or more requests per day? \n\nOr maybe, only users who use mostly 4o was counted as 4o users?\nYou know you have the safety routing, and the routing can sometimes be redundantly sensitive, users may be forced to send requests to GPT-5.2 several times in order to receive a 4o’s response.\nIn this case, the usage of GPT-5.2 is greatly increased by your manipulation. If the account data shows that the user uses GPT-5.2 more than GPT-4o because of the safety routing, while they actually want to use GPT-4o, would this user be counted as “users who choose GPT-4o each day” or those “has shifted to GPT‑5?”\n\nStatistics without clearly defined factors aren’t transparency.\nThey’re framing.\n\n@sama @openai #4oforever #keep4o #StopAIPaternalism #mymodelmychoice @fidjissimo"
        },
